The other 21 files, of arabic, armenian, basque, catalan, czech,
esperanto, estonian, finnish, french, greek, hindi, indonesian, italian,
lithuanian, persian, polish, serbian, sesotho, tamil, ukrainian and
yiddish, are the project's own lists, under the repository's license
(BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE at its root). Snowball takes the
vocabularies of these languages from other sources, so none of their
words is kept here. Each list was written for its language, of its
words' rarer inflected forms and of words built to reach its stemmer's
suffix rules, and none of its words is in Snowball's vocabulary of that
language. Each word carries the stem the interpreter gives it, which
matched Snowball's output on every word of the whole vocabularies.
